cartridge "THE MOST AND THE LEAST/ORSON SCOTT CARD/1986"

' THE MOST AND THE LEAST
' A ColecoVision game based on "The Most and the Least" by Orson Scott
' Card, Ahoy! March 1986 (Commodore 64 BASIC, from his article "Learning
' Is More Fun than Blasting Aliens"; disk ahoy1986-03: the program MOST
' and the four quiz modules MQ US GEOG, MQ US HIST, MQ WHICH and MQ WORLD
' GEOG, orig/). Made for Amy Studio by Claude (an AI made by Anthropic),
' 2026, in Amy by Amy Bienvenu.
'
' The game: choose one of the four quiz modules (U.S. GEOGRAPHY, U.S.
' HISTORY, WHICH IS ..., WORLD GEOGRAPHY). Its eight lists come in a random
' order; each list (7 to 20 entries) is shown in a scrambled order, and you
' build it in the right order, from the top: pick the entry that comes
' next (the longest coast, the first state to ratify, the shortest
' measure...). A right pick scores 10 points for every entry still below
' it (the first of a 20-entry list is worth 190, the second 180, ...); a
' wrong pick costs 10 points and the right entry is shown and put in place
' anyway. Every entry placed shows its fact (miles, dates, people...).
' After the eight lists, the score and the best possible score.
'
' From the original (orig/most.bas, the module listings): the four modules
' with all 32 lists and every entry and fact; the random order of the lists
' and of the entries; picking the next entry from the remaining ones; the
' scoring (QT - NA points for a right pick, -1 for a wrong one, shown times
' ten); a wrong pick shows the right entry and places it; the fact shown
' with each entry placed; the score kept over a module; the menu to resume,
' repeat the group of lists or leave.
'
' Liberties: the 40-column screen is rebuilt for 28 columns: the list has
' the rank and the points of each placed entry, the facts appear on the
' bottom line (the newest one when placed, any one in the review after a
' list), the title is on the line above the facts, and the long titles
' are shortened; the format line and the column
' heads go on an intro card before each list, with notes explaining codes
' and dates. The last entry of a list, the only one left and worth 0, is
' placed by itself. The disk's directory of "Q " files is the menu of the
' four modules (QUIZ MAKER, for making new files, is not ported). The quit
' menu is on the right button (resume, start the module over, back to the
' title). The cursor is a sprite that slides; sounds and a title tune.
' Facts (quizdata.py, CHANGES): errors corrected (Virginia's ratification
' 25 June 1788, Texas seceded 1 February 1861, five Civil War battle dates
' and Chickamauga in Georgia, Appomattox, settlement of Maryland, Delaware,
' New Mexico 1598 and Arizona 1752 (two lists change order), eleven war
' dates, Mondale lost in 1984, Washington had no party, "which planet is
' hottest" is now "nearest", Lake Chad in Africa, Ladoga and Onega in
' Europe, total area not inland area); dated figures kept and marked "as of
' 1986" or with their year on the intro card (populations, areas, the
' USSR, Zaire, Pluto as a dwarf planet since 2006); the author's street
' address in "Which is closest to home" replaced by YOUR HOME.
'
' Controls: either controller. Stick up and down moves the cursor (hold
' to repeat); the left button picks; the right button opens the menu. On
' the title, up and down choose a module, a button starts.
'
' House rules: text in columns 2-29, rows 1-22; tiles from code 128 (128-
' 191 a yellow copy of the font, made at run time; the art from 192); the
' frame loop is protected from the NMI; screens drawn with the NMI off
' after a wait, display off. Music first in the sound table, effects after;
' the title tune is played once. `set sprite count` is always given. Own
' xorshift random numbers. Nothing flashes.

